🚨 **BLOCKING: none** — this file has no blocking findings; see the general review for the full parity verification.

💡 **SUGGESTION: two non-throwing JSON-parse helpers now coexist with different result shapes**

This PR introduces `tryParseJson` in the shared parser module:

```javascript
function tryParseJson(raw) {
    try {
        return { ok: true, value: JSON.parse(raw) };
    } catch (error) {
        console.error('Invalid JSON from AI:', error);
        return { ok: false, value: null };
    }
}
```

`js/createSolutionDesignTicketsAndAssignForReview.js:146` (untouched by this PR) already ships the same "parse AI JSON without throwing" service as `parseAiJson`, returning `{ value }` / `{ error }` with the log left to the caller:

```javascript
function parseAiJson(text) {
    try {
        return { value: JSON.parse(text) };
    } catch (error) {
        return { error: error };
    }
}
```

Both announce the identical `'Invalid JSON from AI:'` contract, so future maintainers now have to know two shapes for one concept. Sharing `tryParseJson` is out of this PR's ticket scope (gh-1191 names six functions and `parseAiJson` lives in a root script), so this is explicitly a follow-up suggestion: consider a later cleanup that moves the shared helper into `js/common/aiResponseParser.js` (it is already exported) and retires `parseAiJson`, keeping the log-on-failure behavior in one place.

No behavior change is requested in this PR — the duplication is pre-existing debt made slightly wider, not introduced.

